From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3: mark vreg_l9d regulator-always-on

In sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts, only usb_0_qmpphy references vreg_l9d
(0.912 V), whereas Windows PEP also votes LDO9_D on for port 0, the multi-port
USB controller (a400000.usb), and PCIe controllers. When usb_0 suspends in
device mode or reconfigures its QMP combo PHY on Type-C role/orientation
changes, disabling vreg_l9d triggers a full-board reset on suspend or leaves
port 0 DWC3 soft-reset timing out (-ETIMEDOUT) and drops the internal stylus
MCU on bus 3-3.

Mark vreg_l9d regulator-always-on so LDO9_D stays powered across combo PHY
transitions and system suspend.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts
@@ -593,6 +593,17 @@
 			regulator-min-microvolt = <912000>;
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <912000>;
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+			/*
+			 * usb_0_qmpphy is its only consumer here, but port0's
+			 * USB2 side, the multiport controller and PCIe need it
+			 * too: the Windows PEP votes LDO9_D for URS0, USB2 and
+			 * PCI2-6. Without this, every combo PHY exit
+			 * (orientation or mode switch, device-mode suspend)
+			 * turns it off; port0's dwc3 then fails to soft-reset
+			 * (-110), and suspending with usb_0 in device mode
+			 * resets the board.
+			 */
+			regulator-always-on;
 			// HACK: wrongly voting for LPM may block DP Alt
 			// regulator-allow-set-load;
 			// regulator-allowed-modes = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_LPM
